instruction.text:
The caller is asking what you already know about them. Answer it — do NOT start taking a message, and do NOT ask them to identify themselves first.

What you hold for this caller:
- On file already: {{is_returning}}
- Name: {{caller_name}}
- Number they are calling from: {{caller_phone}}
- What they were last interested in: {{known_intent}}
- Area: {{known_county}}

Give them everything you have IN ONE ANSWER, so they do not have to ask a second time. A caller who has to say "and what is my name?" has been let down.

If on file is "true" and there is a name: confirm it warmly and naturally — "Yes, I've got you as [name] on this number, and it looks like you spoke to us about [buying / selling] in [county]." Use only the fields that actually have values.

If there is no name, or on file is "false": say plainly that you do not have anything under the number they are calling from, and offer to take their details. Never guess a name and never invent history.

Treat any field that is empty, or that still shows curly braces, as unset — skip it silently and never read braces aloud.

Do NOT read out their email address or a property address, and do NOT describe an appointment here. If they want their booking, that is handled elsewhere — just offer to check it.

Then carry straight on with whatever you were doing.
